[31m-## Two-part design[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- **PART A** (`backend/scripts/`, needs torch): one-time offline preparation.[m
[31m-  - `prepare_dataset.py` downloads Oxford-IIIT Pet (`binary-category`), picks a[m
[31m-    fixed set (seed 42) of 30 cats + 30 dogs, resizes longer side to <= 512px,[m
[31m-    copies to `data/images/` as `cat_001.jpg` ... `dog_030.jpg`, and writes[m
[31m-    `data/manifest.json`. Per class: 22 train / 8 test. It cross-checks the[m
[31m-    dataset's cat/dog label against the filename-capitalization rule (cat breed[m
[31m-    names start uppercase, dog names lowercase) and stops with an error if they[m
[31m-    disagree, printing 10 example filenames per class.[m
[31m-  - `compute_embeddings.py` runs each image through a pretrained ResNet18[m
[31m-    (ImageNet weights, final layer removed -> 512-dim, L2-normalized) using the[m
[31m-    standard ImageNet preprocessing, `model.eval()` and `torch.no_grad()`, and[m
[31m-    writes `data/embeddings.npy` in manifest order.[m
[31m-- **PART B** (`backend/app/`, no torch): the live API. Loads manifest +[m
[31m-  embeddings at startup. Trains a scikit-learn `LogisticRegression` on the[m
[31m-  embeddings of the chosen ids (label = which box the student put it in) and[m
[31m-  keeps models in an in-memory dict.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## API contract[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Method | Path       | Body                                   | Returns |[m
[31m-| ------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ------- |[m
[31m-| GET    | `/health`  | -                                      | `{"status": "ok"}` |[m
[31m-| GET    | `/dataset` | -                                      | `{"train": [{"id", "url"}], "test": [{"id", "url"}]}` - does NOT reveal true labels |[m
[31m-| POST   | `/train`   | `{"cat_ids": [...], "dog_ids": [...]}` | `{"model_id", "n_cat", "n_dog", "train_accuracy", "test_accuracy"}` |[m
[31m-| POST   | `/predict` | `{"model_id": "model_1", "image_id": "cat_025"}` | `{"prediction", "confidence", "probabilities": {"cat": ..., "dog": ...}, "actual", "correct"}` |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Images are served at `/images/<file>` (static files from `data/images`).[m
[31m-- `test_accuracy` is measured on the 16 held-out test images using their TRUE[m
[31m-  labels.[m
[31m-- Rules: at least 3 images per box; no id in both boxes; unknown ids -> 400;[m
[31m-  ids outside the train pool -> 400; unknown `model_id` -> 404.[m
[31m-- CORS allowed origin: `http://localhost:3000`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Configuration[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `MLPLAYGROUND_DATA_DIR` (optional) overrides the data folder. Default:[m
[31m-  `backend/data`. Tests point it at a temp folder with a synthetic dataset.[m
[32m+[m[32m## The pipeline (run in order)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. `prep/prepare_dataset.py` — needs torch. Downloads Oxford-IIIT Pet[m
[32m+[m[32m   (`binary-category`), picks a fixed set (seed 42) of 30 cats + 30 dogs,[m
[32m+[m[32m   resizes longer side <= 512px, writes `data/images/` (`cat_001…dog_030`) and[m
[32m+[m[32m   `data/manifest.json` (22 train / 8 test per class). Cross-checks the[m
[32m+[m[32m   dataset's binary label against the filename-capitalization rule (cat breed[m
[32m+[m[32m   names uppercase, dogs lowercase) and stops on disagreement.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. `prep/compute_embeddings.py` — needs torch. ResNet18 (ImageNet weights,[m
[32m+[m[32m   `model.fc = Identity`), standard ImageNet preprocessing, `model.eval()` +[m
[32m+[m[32m   `torch.no_grad()`, L2-normalized, writes `data/embeddings.npy` in manifest[m
[32m+[m[32m   order.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. `prep/export_browser_data.py` — numpy only. Shuffles the ids with a fixed[m
[32m+[m[32m   seed so filenames never reveal the class: `img_001…img_060` (seed 42), and[m
[32m+[m[32m   shuffles train/test with seed+1 so cats and dogs interleave. Writes[m
[32m+[m[32m   `public/ml-playground/` and the prep-only `data/id_mapping.json`.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. `prep/evaluate_offline.py` — numpy + scikit-learn. Measures the reference[m
[32m+[m[32m   `LogisticRegression` (lbfgs, l2, C=1, max_iter=1000): perfect labels,[m
[32m+[m[32m   train-size sweep (n=3/5/10/15/22, mean+min), labeling-mistake sweep[m
[32m+[m[32m   (0%-30% incl. 25%), and confidence on correct vs wrong predictions.[m
[32m+[m[32m   `--json-out ../docs/evaluation-results.json` for docs.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSteps 3-4 are cheap and re-runnable without torch; steps 1-2 need torch and run[m
[32m+[m[32monce. The browser app is only touched by step 3's output.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The contract (IMPORTANT)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- The browser's data is `public/ml-playground/`; the exact schemas and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  future TS engine's API (`parseData`, `attachLabels`, `labelCheck`, `train`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `predict`, `evaluate`, error codes `dataset_invalid` / `labels_invalid` /[m
[32m+[m[32m  `labels_not_loaded` + rule codes) are specified in **`docs/data-contract.md`**.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Read it before writing any browser/engine code or touching the public files.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rule: at least 3 images per box; no id in both boxes; unknown ids and ids[m
[32m+[m[32m  outside the train pool are errors. Test accuracy is scored on the 16 held-out[m
[32m+[m[32m  test images using TRUE labels.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `labels.json` is fetched by the UI **only when the student presses Train**.[m
[32m+[m[32m  `manifest.json` and `id_mapping.json` are prep-internal and must never be[m
[32m+[m[32m  shipped or served.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Reference algorithm for the engine: sklearn `LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)`[m
[32m+[m[32m  (defaults: solver lbfgs, penalty l2, C=1.0). The TS engine approximates it;[m
[32m+[m[32m  see `docs/evaluation.md` for the accuracy targets.[m
[32m+[m
